## Rulings

Ruling: Task 3 introduces a dedicated `ScrubLeak` carrying `kind`; it does not force `kind` onto ordinary `ScrubSuspect` values — heuristic suspects do not have a replacement kind — if wrong, downstream grouping may need a wider union.

Ruling: no intermediate commits; each task is reviewed from task-local file snapshots and the single authorized commit happens after all gates — preserves the user's dirty related work — if wrong, task-level rollback is less convenient.

Ruling: Tasks 4–6 may revise the same dirty UI files sequentially; later task requirements supersede earlier temporary component shapes while preserving tested interfaces — avoids parallel merge conflicts — if wrong, an intermediate review may flag a gap intentionally completed by the next task.

